#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Magica Terminal — a small VTE terminal where every pane belongs to a Puella Magi character.

Each pane is a VTE terminal with a transparent background layered over a backdrop that draws the
character's HELLO! GOOD SMILE figure in the bottom-right corner, drawn in front of the text. Text, cursor and selection use her
colour. Unfocused panes keep their colours, just less saturated.

Keys
  Ctrl+Shift+O / Ctrl+Shift+E   split right / split down
  Ctrl+Shift+W                  close pane
  Ctrl+Alt+Arrows               move focus between panes
  Ctrl+Shift+T                  new tab          Ctrl+PageUp / PageDown   previous / next tab
  Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V   copy / paste
  Ctrl+Shift+Plus / Minus / 0   bigger / smaller / reset font
  Ctrl+Shift+L                  switch light / dark (remembered; ~/.config/magica-terminal/theme)
  Ctrl+Shift+F                  search the scrollback (Enter older, Shift+Enter newer, Esc close)
  Ctrl+click                    open a link or file path
Typing `pair` (Madoka | Homura) or `magica` (Madoka, Homura above; Sayaka, Mami, Kyoko below) lays out the
tab with those characters; the pane you typed it in becomes Madoka (in a new tab if this one is already split).
Typing `crush` opens Magica Crush, a pixel-art match-3 game with the soul gems, over that pane (Esc / q to go back);
`magica-terminal --crush` does the same inside a pane, and opens a window with it from anywhere else.
In the game, A turns autoplay on or off (CRUSH_AUTOPLAY starts it on); a game it has played doesn't set a best score.
Closing the window saves its tabs, splits, characters and folders (~/.config/magica-terminal/session.json); the
next launch restores them unless another Magica Terminal is open. Exiting the last shell clears it.
After a while with no output or typing, she does a little idle bob or breath now and then.
Hovering the mouse over a figure fades it so the text behind is readable.
A command that fails squashes her and tints her figure and the bar under it red for a moment; one that ran a long time in a pane
you're not looking at makes her hop three times (plus a desktop notification if the window isn't active); any other successful command, one small jump. ~/.bashrc
reports commands to the terminal with VTE's OSC 666 vte.shell.preexec / vte.shell.postexec=<status>.

Settings live in the constants below, and ~/.config/magica-terminal/settings.json can override most of them
(see SETTINGS); figures in figures/<name>.png next to the script.
"""
